        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "439221a3-7b4e-59dc-bc75-2c5ce8893cee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James MacGregor, George V, Queen Victoria, Edward VII\n- Roles: Moderator of the General Assembly of the Church of Scotland, Chaplain in Ordinary, Chaplain, King of the United Kingdom, Emperor of India\n- Organizations: Church of Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- James MacGregor was a Scottish minister and philanthropist who lived from 1832 to 1910.\n- James MacGregor was made Chaplain in Ordinary to Queen Victoria in 1886.\n- James MacGregor was Moderator of the General Assembly of the Church of Scotland in 1891.\n- James MacGregor became Chaplain to King Edward VII in 1901.\n- George V, born George Frederick Ernest Albert, was born on 3 June 1865.\n- James MacGregor became Chaplain to King George V in 1910, serving three monarchs in all.\n- George V became King of the United Kingdom and the British Dominions and Emperor of India on 6 May 1910.\n- James MacGregor died in 1910.\n- George V died on 20 January 1936 after reigning until his death.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
